## Marker forms

The readiness validator reads these byte-exact forms:

```text
RALPH-FACT: <key>: <value>
RALPH-FACT: <key>: RALPH-PENDING (assumed <date>); review trigger: <cond>
RALPH-COMMAND: <approved-tool …>
RALPH-INAPPLICABLE: <reason>
RALPH-PENDING: <approved-tool …> (assumed <date>); review trigger: <cond>
RALPH-REVIEW: <procedure>; evidence: <record>; owner: <role>
```

```text
RALPH-PENDING: pytest (assumed 2026-07-12); review trigger: once test deps are installed
RALPH-FACT: secret_scan_command: RALPH-PENDING (assumed 2026-07-12); review trigger: once a scanner is chosen
```

Start each `RALPH-COMMAND` with an approved tool. A truthful `RALPH-PENDING` entry is an explicit accepted deferral, not an unresolved placeholder. Use `RALPH-INAPPLICABLE` for a permanently irrelevant requirement. For each applicable lint or typecheck language, add `RALPH-LANG: <Language>` and its command, inapplicability declaration, or deferral.

## Complete the corpus

Replace every `RALPH-FACT:` placeholder with verified policy. Remove applied `RALPH-STARTER-TEMPLATE` and `REPLACE-ME` instructions. Finish with no unresolved or completion marker. Resolve Guard inventory Enforcement cells using the enforcement ladder: prefer `deterministic: <id>` where `<id>` resolves to a declared `RALPH-COMMAND:` value or an approved gate command; justify `advisory: <reason>; review: <trigger>` when no deterministic enforcer exists or is feasible. Keep instruction surfaces lean: delete inferable lines first, state qualitative findings rather than unverified numbers or bloat, exclude LLM-generated bulk summaries of the codebase, and do not repeat kernel rules in domain policies. Add a `## Research basis` citation block; give inactive conditional domains dated reactivation triggers; retain `{{ migrated_marker }}` in conventional locations; and keep each policy in its canonical file.

