## Report

Check readiness only with `{{ readiness_check_command | default('python -m ralph.project_policy.check') }}`, never another installed Ralph Workflow, whose rules differ. Finish after resolving every listed finding. Report changed files, migrations, evidence sources, probes, and residual blockers. The runtime then reruns the readiness validator; do not claim completion when a listed finding remains unresolved.

## Three-state readiness (v6)

Current readiness: structure_complete={{ readiness_structure_complete | default('unknown') }}, implementation_verified={{ readiness_implementation_verified | default('unknown') }}, outcome_evidence_reviewed={{ readiness_outcome_evidence_reviewed | default('unknown') }}.
The runtime reports THREE dimensions, not two: structure complete (the validator passes), implementation verified (declared gates ran exit 0 with the current policy-content hash), and outcome evidence reviewed (every declared gate recorded). A structural READY is the caching gate; structural READY is NOT semantic correctness. Your job closes the structural dimension; the runtime and the analysis phase own the other two and surface them in the CLI emit and the status bar footer as `Policy: S*/I*/O*`. Do not present a structural-READY remediation as semantic correctness.
